  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Madagascar (01-Jul-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Madagascar, HIV, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: The number of new HIV infections is reduced by at least 50%, among key populations who are the most exposed to the risk of HIV infection and among the general population, by the end of 2017..  The proportion of HIV-infected infants born to HIV-positive mothers is reduced to less than 5% by the end of 2017..  The proportion of people living with HIV who are alive and on ART at 12 months after treatment initiation is increased to 95% by the end of 2017.. The objectives of this program are: At least 60% of women of childbearing age adopt HIV prevention practices by the end of 2017..  At least 80% of adults and children living with HIV receive medical, psychosocial, social and legal services by the end of 2017..  At least 80% of HIV-positive pregnant women receive a service package to reduce HIV transmission from mother to child by the end of 2017..  At least 80% of the key populations most exposed to HIV, and 60% of people with unstable heterosexual partnerships, adopt behaviours and practices that reduce their risk by the end of 2017..  The risk of HIV transmission through blood transfusion is reduced by at least 50% by the end of 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
